WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.267
-Unbelievable.
She is my jam.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.000
Our next guest won Grammy awards

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.167
for Best New Artist
and Best Jazz Vocal Album.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.267
Performing
"Guess Who I Saw Today,"

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:13.067
from her album "Linger Awhile,"
please welcome, Samara Joy.

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:16.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:22.767
♪♪

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:27.300
-♪ You're so late ♪

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.133
♪ Getting home from the office ♪

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:32.167
♪♪

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:36.534
♪ Did you miss your train? ♪

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:39.100
♪♪

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:48.634
♪ Were you caught in the rain? ♪

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:50.767
♪ No ♪

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:53.667
♪ Don't bother ♪

00:00:53.667 --> 00:01:01.200
♪ Don't bother to explain ♪

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.567
♪ Can I fix you ♪

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:07.234
♪ A quick martini ♪

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:10.167
♪ As a matter of fact ♪

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:16.334
♪ I'll have one with you ♪

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:23.167
♪ For to tell you the truth ♪

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.367
♪ I've had ♪

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:35.367
♪ Quite a day, too ♪

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:39.767
♪♪

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:49.767
♪ Guess who I saw today,
my dear ♪

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:52.367
♪ I went in town ♪

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:57.267
♪ To shop around
for something new ♪

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:02.133
♪ And I thought I'd stop ♪

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:07.934
♪ And grab a bite
when I was through ♪

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:11.033
♪ I looked around ♪

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:16.267
♪ For someplace new ♪

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:19.000
♪ Then it occurred to me ♪

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:24.901
♪ Where I had parked the car ♪

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:34.367
♪ There was a most
attractive French café and bar ♪

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:43.133
♪ It really wasn't very far ♪

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:46.200
♪ The waiter showed me ♪

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:51.601
♪ To a dark, secluded corner ♪

00:02:51.601 --> 00:03:01.567
♪ As my eyes became accustomed
to the gloom ♪

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:04.767
♪ I saw two people at the bar ♪

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:11.300
♪ Who were so much in love ♪

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:20.167
♪ Even I could spot it
clear across the room ♪

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:29.767
♪ Guess who I saw today,
my dear ♪

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:33.234
♪ I'd never been
so shocked before ♪

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:39.601
♪ I headed blindly
through the door ♪

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:48.033
♪ They didn't see me
passing through ♪

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:51.334
♪ Guess who I saw today ♪

00:03:51.334 --> 00:04:00.901
♪ Guess who I saw t-o-o-oday ♪

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:08.701
♪ Guess who I saw today ♪

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:12.534
♪ I ♪

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:20.067
♪ Saw ♪

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:30.067
♪ You ♪

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:38.801
♪♪

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:42.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

